6:242:- **Scope.** A listing leaves out the records Dispatch made for its own use: a ticket's project with everything in it, and a worker session (the planner, an implementer, a reviewer) in any project, told by the `<ticket>-<nonce>` form of the op they were made under (`switchboard_control::is_dispatch_worker_op`). A supervisor's records (`sup-…`) and the owner's own are listed as ever, and a worker record is still read by its id, which is how the ticket view to come will reach them. `?scope=all` on `projects`, `sessions`, `waiting` and on the `events` subscription lists them and announces them; a plain subscription gets no `project`, `sessions`, `session` or `runs` frame about one. `info` lists `scope` among its capabilities. The point is the wire: hundreds of worker sessions on a host, which the headset fetched one project at a time, are now neither fetched nor announced.
9:313:- The pairing window is opened from the settings menu as "Allow pairing for 5 minutes", the same shape as the environment setup window (`ENV_SETUP_WINDOW`, never saved). The dialog that opens it chooses the scope the pairing grants, `read` by default.
10:317:- **A browser's token is a cookie.** `POST /pair` with the additive body field `"transport": "cookie"` answers without `token` and with `Set-Cookie: switchboard_token_<server_id>=<token>; Path=/api/v1/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict`, so script never holds the token and a page on another origin cannot make the browser attach it. The name carries the host's `server_id` because cookies are scoped by host and path, not port, and two instances on one machine would otherwise overwrite each other's token. A request authenticates by its bearer first and otherwise by the cookie of its own host's name; another host's cookie is ignored. A 401 for an unknown token from the host's own cookie (revoked, or every token after a key rotation) clears it with `Max-Age=0`; the refusal text is unchanged, so "revoked" and "never paired" are one answer and the page tells them apart itself. The WebSocket upgrade carries the cookie on the same request. Whether a browser stores a `Secure` cookie from a bypassed-certificate origin is not settled; the page shows "pair again" when its first authenticated call after `/pair` is refused, so a dropped cookie is a visible state.
14:440:**A1 — Identity and an authenticated read-only host.** `identity.json` (id, certificate, `server_name` and the listen preference: off the LAN by default, loopback until enabled), the key in the Keychain under its installation's account, `SWITCHBOARD_REMOTE_PORT`. `ports::remote`, `adapters/remote.rs` with the bounds of §4.1 and the two-step content handoff, a fake, the `Effect` and `AppAction` arms, the allowlist, the redaction function. The pairing window and QR code in the settings menu, the paired-devices dialog with scope and Revoke, `devices.json`. Endpoints: `/info`, `/pair`, projects, spaces, sets, one set, sessions, session, waiting, screen. No events yet; a reply carries `epoch` and `revision` from the counter, which only the diff of A3 will move. The screen is answered on the frame as the control port answers it (a pane snapshot, redacted); the worker handoff arrives with the screen cache of A4, since there is nothing to version before it. *Built 2026-10-12; see design.md's remote client status.* Tests: `tests/remote.rs` against a real socket with fakes, modelled on `tests/control.rs`, covering pairing, the pin check, scope, revocation, the allowlist and screen redaction; a UI test for the dialog. Acceptance: a paired `curl` with the pinned certificate reads every view over the LAN; an unpaired one gets `/info` and nothing else.
16:468:*C1 and C2 built 2026-10-13 (the content endpoints but `file.read`, the conversation paged and merged, the three modes drawn), C3 the same day (`send`, `resume` and `trust` under the control scope through the control socket's `serve` and log, the op the key, `/ops/{op}` on a timeout; a control bar on a Claude session's window with a microphone button that dictates through the Speech framework; the conversation view's place, scroll and folds, kept across merges, reconnects and relaunches); see design.md's remote client status. `file.read` and the policy reads off the frame remain. C4 the same day: `file.read` (`GET projects/{id}/files/{path}`, a file some working set pins, read through the descriptor walk of §4.3 in `adapters::files::open_pinned` on the content worker, versioned by inode, change time and size, masked, refused `not_pinned`, `too_large` with its size, or `failed` for a dotenv file, a symlink or a non-text file) and the policy resolved on the worker: the frame hands the worker what names a policy (`PolicySpec`: the project environment, the sets, an epoch moved by every save and secret change) and the worker reads the dotenv files and the secret store, caching per spec, so a slow Keychain call never costs a frame. Milestone C is complete.*
